
Analysis Description
--------------------
Examine whether or not a codon alignment is better fit by models which
permit multiple instantaneous substitutions. v0.2 adds a separate rate
for codon-island triple-hit rates

- __Requirements__: in-frame codon alignment and a phylogenetic tree

- __Citation__: Submitted; preprint at hyphy.org/resources/fmm.pdf

- __Written by__: Sergei L Kosakovsky Pond, Sadie Wisotsky and Alexander Lucaci

- __Contact Information__: spond@temple.edu

- __Analysis Version__: 1.0


>code => Universal
>Loaded a multiple sequence alignment with **25** sequences, **134** codons, and **1** partitions from `/Users/alex/Documents/selection-tutorial/data/21-empirical/lysin.nex`
The number of omega rate classes to include in the model (permissible range = [1,10], default value = 3, integer): 
>rates => 3

>triple-islands => No


### Obtaining branch lengths and nucleotide substitution biases under the nucleotide GTR model

>kill-zero-lengths => Yes
* Log(L) = -4592.89, AIC-c =  9296.39 (55 estimated parameters)
* 1 partition. Total tree length by partition (subs/site)  2.507

### Obtaining the global omega estimate based on relative GTR branch lengths and nucleotide substitution biases
* Log(L) = -4542.21, AIC-c =  9210.80 (62 estimated parameters)
* 1 partition. Total tree length by partition (subs/site)  2.546
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio for *test* =   0.9328

### Fitting Standard MG94
* Log(L) = -4354.51, AIC-c =  8845.80 (67 estimated parameters)
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio =   1.1464
* The following relative rate distribution (mean 1) for site-to-site **non-synonymous** rate variation was inferred

|               Rate                | Proportion, % |               Notes               |
|-----------------------------------|---------------|-----------------------------------|
|               0.095               |    36.741     |                                   |
|               0.986               |    41.730     |                                   |
|               2.570               |    21.529     |                                   |


### Fitting MG94 with double instantaneous substitutions
* Log(L) = -4295.30, AIC-c =  8729.47 (68 estimated parameters)
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio =   0.9469
* rate at which 2 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon =   0.4614
* The following relative rate distribution (mean 1) for site-to-site **non-synonymous** rate variation was inferred

|               Rate                | Proportion, % |               Notes               |
|-----------------------------------|---------------|-----------------------------------|
|               0.102               |    37.257     |                                   |
|               1.071               |    43.699     |                                   |
|               2.595               |    19.044     |                                   |


### Fitting MG94 with double and triple instantaneous substitutions
* Log(L) = -4292.09, AIC-c =  8725.12 (69 estimated parameters)
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio =   0.9378
* rate at which 2 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon =   0.4010
* rate at which 3 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon =   0.3019
* rate at which 3 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon between synonymous codon islands =   0.3019
* The following relative rate distribution (mean 1) for site-to-site **non-synonymous** rate variation was inferred

|               Rate                | Proportion, % |               Notes               |
|-----------------------------------|---------------|-----------------------------------|
|               0.106               |    37.476     |                                   |
|               1.087               |    43.710     |                                   |
|               2.578               |    18.814     |                                   |


